{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonfoodietours/items/259015/", "pk": 259015, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonfoodietours/", "pk": 61385, "shortname": "bostonfoodietours", "name": "Boston Foodie Tours", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Beacon Hill Neighborhood Tour - Private Tour", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 11, "unicode": "Beacon Hill Neighborhood Tour - Private Tour", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": false, "sold_out_text": "", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 2.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 2.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 3000, "description": "#Get fancy without dressing fancy! \n\n## Duration\n4 hours\n\n## About Boston Foodie Tours\nNamed Massachusetts' #1 Food Tour by Yelp (2025), locally owned Boston Foodie Tours (“BFT”) focuses on award-winning best eats, culinary education, and the city’s rich history. We partner with Best of Boston winners, James Beard Award winners, food institutions, and the like. \n\n## Beacon Hill Neighborhood Tour\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nOur private Beacon Hill Neighborhood Tour is most appropriate for small groups, and offers two upscale restaurant dining experiences. \n\nWith its Federal brick townhouses, window boxes, gas-lit street lamps, cobblestone streets, and brick sidewalks, historic Beacon Hill is a must-visit for both locals and tourists.\n\nOur tour begins at Scampo, the restaurant of a legendary James Beard Award winner, Lydia Shire. Here, guests will be served a mozzarella-tomato salad with an aged balsamic vinegar,  and Chef's iconic lobster pizza.\n\nNext, guests will enjoy a small ice cream of choice at a local ice shop ranked by GQ magazine as one of the top ten in the country that you must try. Tastings of top-selling chocolate truffles at a multiple \"Best of Boston Chocolatiers\" follows.\n\nThe sightseeing portion of the tour will bring our guests to Acorn Street, described as the most photographed street in Boston, and sometimes the country! Next, we'll visit historic Louisburg Square, the home of John Kerry, among other past and present literary notables. \n\nOur tour route will intersect with the Black Heritage Trail, where you'll find a significant part of Beacon Hill's history, including the Museum of African American History, the oldest standing Black church building in the country.\n\nOur tour will proceed to a popular Beacon Hill nuts shop, where a surprise awaits, and to a multiple Best of Boston-winning chocolate shop, where guests will enjoy a demo of top-selling truffles.\n\nA lovely stroll through the Boston Public Garden, the oldest botanical garden in the country, will lead to the tour finale: two courses at award-winning French restaurant, Bistro du Midi.\n\n## Additional Tour Considerations\n- Depending on the day of the week, the route may be reversed to accommodate restaurant opening times.\n\n- Currently, we can only offer this tour in the afternoon due to restaurant schedules. \n\n-Tastings amount to a full meal.\n\n-Tour requires the physical ability to climb a hill.\n\n-Tour can  accommodate most dietary restrictions well.\n\n- Not recommended for young children.\n\n## What to Bring\n- A bottle of water.\n- Cash to purchase drinks and for your guide gratuity!\n- Please wear comfortable walking shoes.", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "Beacon Hill, Boston", "booking_notes": "### Additional Information\n- Tours require a minimum of four guests in order to run as scheduled. Should we not meet our sales requirement, you will be offered the opportunity to transfer your tickets to another tour, or to receive a full refund.\n- We defer to parents' judgment as to whether our tours are appropriate for their children. Children two years of age and under are free of charge. Over two years of age are charged full price.\n- While we can't assure guests that we'll be able to accommodate all dietary restrictions, we are more able to do so with advance notice. Thank you for completing the questionnaire at checkout fully so that we can ensure an optimal tour experience. This tour does not accommodate vegan dietary restrictions. \n- This tour requires the physical ability to walk up to one and a half miles with frequent stops.\n\n### What to Bring\n- Bottle of water\n- Cash to purchase drinks and to tip your guide (option to pre-pay gratuity at check out)!\n- Please wear comfortable walking shoes\n\n*Should you have questions relative to the this tour, please contact us directly at info@bostonfoodietours.com or at (617) 461-5772.*", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "4 Hours", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonfoodietours/items/259015/images/693324/", "pk": 693324, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/E1Ralv5RxKnFDRGQRQOA", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/E1Ralv5RxKnFDRGQRQOA", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonfoodietours/"}, "item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonfoodietours/items/259015/"}, "crop": {}, "cropped_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/E1Ralv5RxKnFDRGQRQ